{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794488950,"nonce":"EbfFp0/n96SQ5DxJ57Ksj5DfnIQ=","title":"x","message":"`scarab validate` reports `lib:` library steps as \"not checked (use --server to check them)\" even when `--server` is given. The server does check them, so the output points at a check that already happened.\n\nFound 2026-11-12 on v0.4.0 (main 8ca029fb). I checked a devops-gitops Pipeline that invokes `lib:thulasi-ram/build` against the kind stack, whose org has the library installed.\n\nObserved:\n\n    $ scarab validate .scarab/ci-tools-image.yaml --server http://127.0.0.1:8090 \\\n        --org scarab-admin --project scarab-admin/scarab-libs --event pull_request --pr 1\n    unresolved: `lib:thulasi-ram/build` is installed on the server, not on disk; its Steps were              not checked (use --server to check them)\n    unresolved: `lib:thulasi-ram/clone` is installed on the server, not on disk; its Steps were              not checked (use --server to check them)\n    ok: 3 step(s), ir v3\n    no run.create Policy applies\n    outcome: allow\n\nCause:\n1. `crates/scarab-cli/src/validate.rs` `run()` calls the offline `compile()` on the `--server` path too, and `compile()` always prints the \"unresolved ... use --server\" lines.\n2. The server compiles the Pipeline against the org's installations (`policies.rs` `pipeline_input`, `installed_libraries` then `compile_bounded`). That compile succeeded, but the CLI prints nothing to say so.\n3. `ok: 3 step(s)` counts the offline IR, in which each library is one stub. The Run would have 5 steps: checkout/git, amd64/image, amd64/push, arm64/image, arm64/push.\n4. The message string is missing a `\\` line continuation, so it prints a run of spaces between \"were\" and \"not\" (validate.rs:180).\n\nExpected, with `--server`:\n- No \"not checked\" lines for libraries the server resolved, or a line saying the server compiled them.\n- The step count from the server's compile.\n- An error naming the library when it is not installed in `--org`. I have not checked what the server answers in that case.\n\nOpen question: does the policy-test path also apply the library trust invariants that Run creation applies (the `Sandbox` refusal when the source is not trusted for `build_sandbox`, `ForgeToken`)? `pipeline_input` runs `admission_before_policies`, which covers Environment governance. I did not confirm whether trust is checked there. If it is not, `--server` can say `outcome: allow` for a Run that Run creation refuses for missing trust. To be useful before an upgrade to 0.4.0, validate should report that refusal too.\n\nWorkaround used: a throwaway test that calls `trigger_runs_from_event` with the real libs/build.yaml and libs/clone.yaml installed in `InMemoryLibraries`.","files":null}]}